			{" "}
			<p>{"I’m happy to announce the "}<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href={"https://unpkg.com/browse/htmx.org@1.0.0/"}>1.0.0 release</a>{" of htmx."}</p>
			{" "}
			<p>{"htmx is now mature enough that I can recommend it as a general replacement for intercooler.js projects. I "}<strong>don’t</strong>{" think there is a strong reason to port an existing intercooler project to htmx. I have several large intercooler apps and will not be moving them over any time soon. I can, however, recommend using htmx over intercooler for new projects."}</p>
			{" "}
			<p>{"htmx is a different sort of javascript library. It is an HTML & hypertext-oriented reply to the current dominance of javascript-based SPA libraries. It is a response to Tom MacWright’s question: "}<a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://macwright.com/2020/10/28/if-not-spas.html">“If not SPAs, What?”</a>.</p>
			{" "}
			<p>{"As the "}<a href="https://htmx.org/">homepage says</a>:</p>
			{" "}
